Reconcile the preceding reference-contract, ordinary-state, lifecycle and protocol audits into one authoritative execution-ready migration and acceptance matrix for objective /05. Read all artifacts and resolve conflicting ownership proposals, duplicate domains, uncovered transport paths and assumptions about change-flag consumers, cross-domain coherence or lifetime. Trace any disputed producer/consumer in code; where behavior cannot be established statically, specify or perform a focused permitted investigation rather than selecting an unsupported design. Ask for user direction when a substantive product or architectural tradeoff remains unresolved.

Each final matrix row must identify the old transport and source references; authoritative backend owner and mutation publisher; proposed canonical UnlockedData domain; TuiFrontEnd projection and refresh outputs; unknown/change semantics; thread, identity and lifecycle rules; action/event control obligations; migration goal; obsolete code removed by that goal; and concrete tests demonstrating equivalence. Account for every initial runtime option and callback return inventoried, every transported Snapshot and non-Snapshot state bypass, and every remaining backend dependency in TUI. Explicitly distinguish frontend-local ComposerSnapshot/editor undo/projection copies and backend-internal snapshots from prohibited backend-to-TUI transfers. Verify that this distinction is based on actual producers and consumers, not naming.

Update the descriptions of /05/02 through /05/09 directly where investigation changes their scope, dependencies, interfaces or verification requirements. Keep the migration incremental and buildable, with each slice deleting its superseded delivery path and no indefinite dual authorities. Document temporary bridges with precise removal ownership and ensure the final design has none. Define boundary checks that prevent regression without a blanket name ban, and record a focused-test/terminal-smoke acceptance matrix plus final full-suite requirements. Store the consolidated artifacts with contents entries. The parent audit is complete only when all paths have an owner, a migration destination and a verification criterion, and blocking design questions are resolved or explicitly returned to the user; no production migration is performed in this goal.
